{"id": "EUVD-2026-76597", "enisaUuid": "edd521d2-ef82-305e-84cf-95303409ac15", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: fix clock domain mismatch in clients_still_reclaiming()\n\nclients_still_reclaiming() computes a deadline from nn->boot_time\n(CLOCK_REALTIME, ~1.7 billion) but compares it against\nktime_get_boottime_seconds() (CLOCK_BOOTTIME, seconds since boot).\nThe comparison is always false \u2014 it would take ~54 years of uptime\nfor BOOTTIME to exceed the REALTIME-derived deadline.\n\nThis means any client can hold the server in grace indefinitely by\nsending CLAIM_PREVIOUS OPEN requests, blocking all non-reclaim\noperations for all other clients.\n\nAdd boot_time_bt (CLOCK_BOOTTIME) alongside the existing boot_time\nand use it for the deadline computation. boot_time (CLOCK_REALTIME)\nis preserved for its cl_boot clientid-nonce role.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:20", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04c3e4456fe76e8d7c94171009df3165c3262c51", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e92e80c5b043108029bc729b30d12c37158fb9cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9cec313efb2fd18d962aad738a4892bce806016", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9843649196221152b6e5d138a3ce859bdaae1d96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09ea3eb9a518565f5bca386e81b993ed8825f5e8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3574-3v33-rcrf", "CVE-2026-89685"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3d5b7535-9649-3a60-8cea-4ff78a5ed59d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "20b7d86f29d39e8ae19bb29c24ffee70dc385ddf <f9cec313efb2fd18d962aad738a4892bce806016"}, {"id": "6fe700c1-3484-3bb0-b57c-523060606382", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "20b7d86f29d39e8ae19bb29c24ffee70dc385ddf <9843649196221152